> Important Keybinds

the most important keybind to know is *SUPER+K*

this will open a searchable menu with all of your keybinds.

whenever SUPER is noted in your keybinds, that's the button between ctrl and alt. on most keyboards it has a windows logo, on macOS it'll be the option key.

However, you don't want to be referencing this menu all the time, so here's the keybinds you should learn first:

[^SUPER+SPACE]:
opens your app runner, also set up to find files within your home directory and find DMS settings.

[^SUPER+Y]:
opens shelly, your package installer GUI. first time you can pick which repositories (pacman + AUR recommended, flatpak optional).

*super+shift+Y* opens the unipkg TUI (if installed), which works on non-arch distros.

[^SUPER+R]:
reloads mango config, important after changing config files.

[^SUPER+1-9]:
switch between workspaces. hold SHIFT to move the active window with you.

[^SUPER+Q]:
closes the current window (like pressing X on a desktop window).

[^SUPER+Z]:
opens the power menu (logout/reboot/shutdown).

[^SUPER+E]:
opens your file browser (nautilus).

[^SUPER+B]:
opens firefox.

[^SUPER+ENTER]:
opens your terminal (ghostty).

[^SUPER+H]:
opens command help TUI with TLDR summaries and man page access.

[^SUPER+SHIFT+H]:
opens this help system.

[^SUPER+X]:
opens process manager / performance monitor (CPU/RAM/disk usage, kill frozen programs).

[^SUPER+K]:
full keybind overview, searchable.

[^SUPER+W]:
wallpaper selector (choose wallpaper groups).

[^SUPER+M]:
mango config editor TUI.

[^SUPER+Left Mouse]:
drag and re-organize windows.

[^SUPER+Right Mouse]:
drag to re-size windows.

[^SUPER+T]:
toggle float/unfloat active window.

[^SUPER+F]:
toggle fullscreen.

[^SUPER+C]:
toggle scratchpad.

[^SUPER+ALT+SPACE]:
toggle terminal scratchpad (quick-access ghostty).
